  "title": "Hamiltonian cycles in line graphs of infinite graphs",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Conjecture\n\n- If $G$ is a 4-edge-connected locally finite graph, then its line graph is hamiltonian.\n- If the line graph $L(G)$ of a locally finite graph $G$ is 4-connected, then $L(G)$ is hamiltonian.",
